            <ArticleTitle>[Diagnostic ultrasonography of the sternoclavicular joint].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>74-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To evaluate the value of ultrasonography in the diagnosis of swelling and lesions of the sternoclavicular joint (SCG).</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="MATERIAL AND METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">We analysed the sonograms of 20 SCG of 18 patients with pain and swelling of the SCG. Ultrasonography was performed just after the clinical examination, using a 7.5 MHz linear scanner.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">All examinations of the SCG produced distinct and clear sonographical findings. We showed that luxations of the SCG as well as tumors and local inflammation can be identified.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Ultrasonographic examination is a noninvasive, time sparing and economical diagnostic tool for clarifying the differential diagnosis of lesions of the SCG and establish may a therapy regimen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
